#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157271 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "706303c1-0e4c-55f7-8b62-5094938f85bc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Function of a Jordan Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fe7ce25-0b30-58c2-bf63-9503ead7b997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2e & {e}^{3}-4e \\\\ e & {e}^{3}-2e\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413963} {:answer/id #uuid "771abe02-8516-59d0-acc3-5894347ab301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3}+2e & -4e \\\\ e & {e}^{3}-2e\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413969} {:answer/id #uuid "86191a40-b259-50e8-a428-ed6d4258f5b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3e & -4e \\\\ e & -e\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413972} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f65777-1fc0-5be0-b73c-a38fdbb7f26f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3} & -4{e}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{3} & -{e}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413976} {:answer/id #uuid "c1499551-986a-5c17-a47d-1c94feaf79fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3{e}^{3} & 2{e}^{3} \\\\ 2{e}^{3} & -{e}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1f65777-1fc0-5be0-b73c-a38fdbb7f26f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3} & -4{e}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{3} & -{e}^{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413976} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc2ff6f6-b56f-5924-a7f7-5f180522f2b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e45b0296-d991-5cc8-b0d3-09c2315c742d" :question/math-academy-id "q-252923" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,J=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven that $B=PJ{P}^{-1},$ find ${e}^{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and matrices $A$ and $S,$ where $S$ is invertible, we have\n\n$$\nf(SA{S}^{-1})=S\\cdot f(A)\\cdot {S}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFor $f(x)={e}^{x}$ and the given matrix $B,$ we have\n\n$$\n{e}^{B}={e}^{PJ{P}^{-1}}=P\\cdot ({e}^{J})\\cdot {P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nNow, since $J$ is a Jordan block with $3$s on the main diagonal, we have\n\n$$\nf(J)=[\\begin{aligned}f(3) & {f}^{′}(3) \\\\ 0 & f(3)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $f$ is ${f}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{e}^{J}=[\\begin{aligned}f(3) & {f}^{′}(3) \\\\ 0 & f(3)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3} & {e}^{3} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAlso, the inverse of $P$ is\n\n$$\n{P}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{B} & =P\\cdot ({e}^{J})\\cdot {P}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3} & {e}^{3} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & {e}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{3} & -2{e}^{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3} & -4{e}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{3} & -{e}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157269 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ce12d6f-8d1c-52f3-992f-534b9d91dda9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Function of a Jordan Block"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7017ca3d-0bfe-52d1-9050-c702cd83a55e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7017ca3d-0bfe-52d1-9050-c702cd83a55e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413967} :answer-field/id #uuid "1be2dfa0-21be-544d-a1f5-2b91c1394fc1" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413984} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50e684f7-c0dc-543a-9c28-178ef40b05b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50e684f7-c0dc-543a-9c28-178ef40b05b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413961} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bc444ac-61d1-5d9d-a293-e4884a3c6bdc" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413986} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ac65ddc-f414-5326-a3bc-41c77e6c0772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ac65ddc-f414-5326-a3bc-41c77e6c0772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413966} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dfbf7ac-1fc0-56fc-a408-ebb0747f3e8b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413991} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92e07177-3942-5994-aa2e-0f158743cebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92e07177-3942-5994-aa2e-0f158743cebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413974} :answer-field/id #uuid "abfbe20d-975b-5409-836a-63b3ba3fd14e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413993} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4708abe6-6e16-586d-9376-e4cd2a6263c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4708abe6-6e16-586d-9376-e4cd2a6263c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413958} :answer-field/id #uuid "d256b7bd-d82f-5eea-9029-63d551e9784e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7c9cc08-2f20-518c-b5b2-1d66ba20819d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7c9cc08-2f20-518c-b5b2-1d66ba20819d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413977} :answer-field/id #uuid "dacae818-b103-5f5c-a483-27a1678df333" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a64ad91-1a79-5d6b-9232-aac7246f71fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-253321" :question/problem "Let ${J}_{n}(\\lambda )$ denote an $n\\times n$ Jordan block with $\\lambda $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${e}^{{J}_{3}(1)}=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-6}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=[\\begin{aligned}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $f(x)={e}^{x},$ $n=3,$ and $\\lambda =1.$\n\nSince $n=3,$ we need to compute the first $3-1=2$ derivative of $f:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & ={e}^{x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{3}(1)) & =[\\begin{aligned}f(1) & {f}^{′}(1) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2!} \\\\ 0 & f(1) & {f}^{′}(1) \\\\ 0 & 0 & f(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}e & e & \\frac{e}{2} \\\\ 0 & e & e \\\\ 0 & 0 & e\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157269 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ce12d6f-8d1c-52f3-992f-534b9d91dda9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Function of a Jordan Block"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f52e38a-24e3-5e4b-ac01-1a4c1fa10cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f52e38a-24e3-5e4b-ac01-1a4c1fa10cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921